# Local development overrides. Copy this file into the app you are running:
#
#     cp .env.local.example apps/flow/.env.local
#
# IMPORTANT: it must go in `apps/<app>/`, not the repo root. Every app sets
# Vite's `root` to its own directory and none of them set `envDir`, so Vite
# loads env files from `apps/<app>/` only. A `.env.local` at the repo root is
# read by nothing.
#
# `.env.local` is gitignored. `.env.local.example` is not - keep secrets out of
# this file, and remember every `VITE_*` var is inlined into the browser bundle.
#
# Restart the dev server after changing this file; Vite reads env at boot.

# ---- API ---------------------------------------------------------------
# THE ONE THAT MATTERS. Unset, every app falls back to the hosted default
# (https://api.voxire.com/) - so a dev server with no `.env.local` reads AND
# WRITES production data. `apiTargetGuardPlugin` prints a banner at startup
# whenever this resolves to a non-loopback host.
#
# Point it at your local onion instance. onion's default dev port is 9999;
# check `~/Development/onion` if you have changed it.
VITE_API_URL=http://localhost:9999/

# ---- Environment -------------------------------------------------------
# Tags Sentry/PostHog events. Keep local work out of the production buckets.
VITE_APP_ENV=development

# ---- Observability -----------------------------------------------------
# Leave both blank locally. Populated values send your dev session's errors
# and analytics to the real projects.
VITE_SENTRY_DSN=
VITE_POSTHOG_KEY=

# ---- Feature flags -----------------------------------------------------
# Only set these to override what you get by default. Resolution order is
# PostHog -> VITE_APP_*_ENABLED -> FLAG_PROD_DEFAULTS (see
# `packages/config/src/flags.ts`).
#
# Do NOT copy the flag block out of `.env.example` - its values are all `0`,
# which switches OFF six app surfaces that are ON in production and will send
# you debugging a blank page. Leave them unset unless you are deliberately
# testing a flag.
#
# VITE_APP_ERP_ENABLED=1
# VITE_APP_CRM_ENABLED=1

# ---- Auth --------------------------------------------------------------
# Only needed if you are working on the "Continue with Google" button.
# VITE_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=
